# pdxcurl -- caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none.
#
# pdxcurl's role: capability-native improved-curl (paideia-os
# design/networking/pdxcurl-design.md §8 + design/networking/
# r100-user-tools-plan.md §12.3). At v1.1.0 the tool body is a
# STUB argv-refusing entry with the v1.1-B semantic-pipe emission
# wire landed (pdxcurl#21) -- real M2/M3 (HTTP-only GET, TLS
# handshake, audit INTENT/RESULT pair) is tracked as pdxcurl#5..#12
# and blocked on libpdx-net M5 landing the net_tls_wrap /
# net_connect wire. The caps.decl is authored at v1.1.0 to the
# design-doc-final surface so no caps.decl churn is needed as M2/M3
# real bodies land.
#
# Kind rationale:
#   KIND_USER          -- invoker attribution (audit record identity);
#                         every satellite in the R100 wave lists this.
#   KIND_TLS_TRUST     -- optional. v1.4.0 (Wave HH, pdxcurl#8) lands
#                         the --trust=cap:<n> argv gate + a WEAK-stub
#                         net_tls_wrap call (src/tls_wire.pdx), but
#                         <n> is stored as an opaque u64 and never
#                         resolved against a live capability table --
#                         pdxtrust M1 (cap mint) and libpdx-net M5
#                         (real handshake) are still both UNAVAILABLE
#                         per STATUS.md. Stays optional until a real
#                         enforcement point exists; promoting it to
#                         mandatory ahead of that would refuse every
#                         https:// invocation for a claim this landing
#                         cannot back up. Placeholder 0x1A7 per parent
#                         plan §12.3 (mirrored as TlsWire::KIND_TLS_
#                         TRUST, documentation-only).
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT  -- optional; documentation-only at v1.1-B.
#                         The v1.1-B semantic-pipe emission wire
#                         uses sys_semantic_send (SC+ ID 115) which
#                         takes NO cap slot. Retained for a future
#                         KIND_SEMANTIC_PIPE recv-side cap.
#   KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL -- deliberately absent from this decl per
#                         design/networking/pdxcurl-design.md §8:
#                         no elevate gate on an HTTP/HTTPS client
#                         request at v1.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit)
 KIND_TLS_TRUST          0x001   # optional -- v1.4.0 wires --trust=cap:<n> + a WEAK-stub net_tls_wrap
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # optional -- documentation-only (see above)
